     "Record the claims bar date and the order or notice that establishes it. Note whether the date applies to all creditors or only to a defined group. Record the date the firm received the order and the person who read it. A date copied without its scope can be applied too broadly.",
     "Record any separate deadline for governmental units, secured creditors, or claims arising after the petition date. These groups often have different treatment under the rules. Record the source paragraph for each date. The lawyer confirms which deadline applies to a given creditor.",
     "Record the claims agent, the filing portal, and the address for a mailed claim. Note the version of the instructions in use at intake. A portal that changed its fields can produce a rejected claim. The log should show where the claim was actually filed."
